WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:21.594
A servant led Kopp and Humm into the throne room.

2
00:00:23.095 --> 00:00:25.296
The king explained his daughter's condition.

3
00:00:26.097 --> 00:00:29.078
The two wise philosophers listened carefully.

4
00:00:29.098 --> 00:00:32.616
"Now tell us," the king said.

5
00:00:32.636 --> 00:00:36.439
"What is the cure for our daughter's problem?"

6
00:00:37.539 --> 00:00:38.860
Kopp spoke up first.

7
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.301
"I know what's wrong.

8
00:00:42.502 --> 00:00:44.803
The princess' soul is in the wrong body."

9
00:00:45.884 --> 00:00:47.725
The queen blinked in surprise.

10
00:00:47.745 --> 00:00:49.686
"I don't understand."

11
00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:54.188
"Let me explain," Kopp said.

12
00:00:54.208 --> 00:01:00.192
"When babies are born, they must wait for their souls to arrive.

13
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.821
This takes some time.

14
00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:08.144
And I think the wrong soul arrived in the princess' body."

15
00:01:08.164 --> 00:01:10.866
"What on earth are you talking about?"

16
00:01:11.206 --> 00:01:12.147
the king snapped.

17
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:21.393
"Earth? No, Your Majesty, I'm talking about a different planet.

18
00:01:22.774 --> 00:01:25.856
I believe Ellen's soul came from the planet Mercury.

19
00:01:28.078 --> 00:01:30.380
But don't worry," Kopp said quickly.

20
00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:33.185
"There's a simple cure for this problem."

21
00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:36.367
"Whew!" The king smiled.

22
00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:38.408
"Finally some good news."

23
00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:40.469
"Please tell us."

24
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:41.830
The queen begged him.

25
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.071
"How can we cure her?"

26
00:01:45.312 --> 00:01:48.414
"You must teach her all about our planet," Kopp said.

27
00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:51.576
"She must learn about our animals and plants."

28
00:01:52.716 --> 00:01:53.817
He tapped his chin.

29
00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:59.040
"And of course someone must also teach her about art and literature.

30
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.623
It will take time, but—" "No no no!"

31
00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:06.024
Humm roared.

32
00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:08.705
"That's completely wrong!

33
00:02:10.726 --> 00:02:12.107
It's my turn now.

34
00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:18.470
And I know exactly what's wrong with the princess.

35
00:02:20.672 --> 00:02:28.356
There's a problem with her her blood."

36
00:02:29.536 --> 00:02:30.377
"Her blood?"

37
00:02:30.797 --> 00:02:31.578
the queen said.

38
00:02:31.598 --> 00:02:35.320
"Yes." Humm nodded.

39
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.804
"Her blood is flowing through her body in the wrong direction.

40
00:02:42.225 --> 00:02:44.506
That's why she lacks gravity.

41
00:02:45.927 --> 00:02:47.769
I don't know what caused it.

42
00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:52.612
To cure her, you must first put her in a warm bath.

43
00:02:53.452 --> 00:02:57.135
Then you'll need air pumps and—" "Enough!"

44
00:02:57.475 --> 00:02:58.296
the king cried.

45
00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:00.977
"You may be wise philosophers.

46
00:03:01.157 --> 00:03:03.278
But your ideas are ridiculous!"

47
00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:05.099
The queen nodded.

48
00:03:05.119 --> 00:03:09.002
"Why don't you two stay at the palace for a few days.

49
00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.423
Watch the princess closely.

50
00:03:11.503 --> 00:03:13.104
Then tell us what you think."

51
00:03:15.906 --> 00:03:19.107
And so the two philosophers moved into the palace.

52
00:03:22.109 --> 00:03:26.452
Now, reader, what did Ellen do when the philosophers began watching her?

53
00:03:30.696 --> 00:03:33.583
Why, she laughed at them, of course!
